NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_THEME_BASE_DROPDOWN="false"

# PASS2D (FRONTEND-1): every saved theme in the composer's "My themes" list shows colour chips like the presets do (PASS2-J4-FINDINGS item 6a). Exact "true" plus the Studio shell enables it;
# default off, and then the list is exactly as before. READ AT BUILD TIME: set it on Vercel, then redeploy. Needs the composer dropdowns (NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_COMPOSER_POPUPS_V2); the older flat
# list is untouched. On, a theme saved on a preset shows that preset's chips (title ground, brand, accent, text, surface, background), read from Theme Builder's own preset contract
# (GET /api/v1/themes/presets/{id}, one read-only call per preset per page load, the same call the deck Theme dialog makes) with the theme's own colour overrides laid over them; a custom
# theme shows the colours it names. Until Theme Builder answers, or if it cannot, a row keeps the chip it had (its explicit primary colour, or none). The list, the selection and every
# handler are the same.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_THEME_SAVED_CHIPS="false"

# PASS2D (FRONTEND-1): the Themes & brand preview draws a preset in Theme Builder's own canon colours (PASS2-J4-FINDINGS item 5). Exact "true" plus the Studio shell enables it; default off, and then
# the preview is exactly as before. READ AT BUILD TIME: set it on Vercel, then redeploy. On, the specimen, the saved-theme swatches and the custom-colour placeholders take a preset's background, surface,
# brand, accent and heading colours from Theme Builder's own preset contract (GET /api/v1/themes/presets/{id}, one read-only call per preset per page load, the call the deck Theme dialog makes), so
# Gilded Noir previews near-black with gold and Minimal black with red, as in the builder, and a canon-only preset is never drawn in Corporate Light's blue. Until Theme Builder answers (or if it
# cannot) a preset keeps the older guide palette it had, and a canon-only preset a neutral grey. Words, colours and nothing else: the saved theme and the payload are the same.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_THEME_PREVIEW_CANON="false"

