# PASS2 ONBOARDING (FRONTEND-1, the /onboarding wizard): exact "true" enables it; default off, and then the page is exactly as before. Needs the Studio shell (NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_V4_SHELL "true"; its "Use a template"
# opens the shell's template library); without it the old page renders untouched. READ AT BUILD TIME: set it on Vercel, then redeploy. On, /onboarding is the same five steps (welcome, use, role, team, starting
# point) in the Studio shell's palette, type and spacing, light and dark, with the choices as real radio groups and a visible "Choose one to continue." instead of a silently disabled button. What changes, and why:
# the dead "Try these prompts" buttons are a plain list; "Profile personalized", "AI agents ready to collaborate", "Enterprise features available ... SSO", "Recommended for you" and "just 4 quick steps"
# (over "Step 1 of 5") are gone, because the page stores nothing and recommends nothing; the 1 s fake "Processing..." wait is gone; the dialog is a last screen with a recap; "2025" in two example prompts is "next
# year"; "Use a template" opens /studio/templates (not the public gallery); "Skip" says where it goes. Nothing is sent or stored; role and team size are still only repeated in the recap. The Studio introduction
# (OnboardingModal) and the cinematic intros are not changed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_ONBOARDING="false"

# PASS2 POLISH PP-1..PP-8 (FRONTEND-1, ops/program/cards/FE-P2-POLISH-FROM-SHOTS.md): exact "true" enables all eight; default off, and then every page is exactly as before. READ AT BUILD TIME: set it on
# Vercel, then redeploy. Each fix also needs its page's own Pass 2 flag, so with this on and a page's flag off, that page is untouched: (PP-1/2/3, NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_PUBLISH plus the Studio shell)
# the publish wizard no longer lays its sticky footer over the "What viewers get" panel (the step and the panel scroll on their own above it), "View as a viewer" takes the shell's action colour
# instead of violet, and the manage view ends with a Done button that closes the dialog; (PP-4, NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_LANDING) the open phone menu dims the page behind it and, at 520px and
# below, is a sheet under the header instead of a card over the headline; (PP-5/PP-7, NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_INTELLIGENCE) the model comparison panel scrolls inside the window so the note is never cut
# mid-line over "Use this model", and "Managed by Deckster" is four columns from 1200px; (PP-6, NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_PROFILE_MENU) when the quota read fails the account menu keeps the plan badge
# (from the session's tier) and says "Usage unavailable" in the capacity card; (PP-8, the same menu flag) the account menu's vertical rhythm is tighter: 32px rows (were 38), 8px between
# sections with one hairline (above Sign out) instead of three, and a tighter capacity card (the Appearance control is as it was).
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_POLISH="false"

# PASS3 DUPLICATE A DECK (FRONTEND-2, Studio half; Layout half is layout-builder-v7.5 !244, POST /api/presentations/{id}/duplicate behind LAYOUT_PRESENTATION_DUPLICATE_ENABLED): exact "true"
# enables it; default off, and then the deck list's disabled "Duplicate" item and its note are exactly as before. READ AT BUILD TIME: set it on Vercel, then redeploy. Do NOT turn it on
# until the Layout endpoint is live in the same environment: Layout answers 404 while its own flag is off, and Studio then shows "Duplicating decks is not available in this environment yet"
# and creates nothing. On: a deck's card menu has a working Duplicate for decks that have a Layout presentation (disabled with a short reason otherwise). Click: (1) Layout copies the deck
# (client operation_id, title "<title> (copy)"); (2) POST /api/sessions makes the copy's session; (3) PATCH /api/sessions/{id} stores the copy's URL and id in the slot the original used
# (final or strawman), currentStage, slideCount, lastMessageAt and the marker stateCache.currentStatus.copiedFrom = { sessionId, title }. If (2) or (3) fails the new session is soft-deleted and
# the person is told "The copy could not be finished." and that a stray Layout copy may remain (the browser cannot delete a Layout deck). Chat history is NOT copied: Director has no session
# clone, so the copy opens as a new session over the copied deck and its chat starts fresh with one line, "Copied from <original title>. Chat history stays with the original."
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_DUPLICATE_DECK="false"

# PASS2 Profile page (FRONTEND-1, /settings/profile; there is no mockup for it): an exact "true" turns it on; default off, and then the page is exactly as before. Needs the Studio shell
# (NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_V4_SHELL "true"); without it the classic page renders untouched. READ AT BUILD TIME: set it on Vercel, then redeploy. On: the profile card in the shell's tokens and type
# (17px title, 12px body, light and dark), sentence-case labels, the initials circle in the palette's teal (no purple-to-blue gradient), a visible "Change photo" button with the accepted types and
# size (the old camera overlay showed on hover only, so a phone could not find it), a name or photo that cannot be saved is said in plain words (the old page showed the server's raw words such as
# "Unauthorized" or "Failed to upload avatar", a JSON parse error for an unreadable reply, and "Failed to fetch"), "Display name saved." / "Account photo saved." after a save, a loading shape, and a
# signed-out message with a "Sign in" link instead of a blank page. "Save" is the ink action colour (as NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_ACCOUNT makes it on the old page). The same three things as before:
# display name, account photo, the way to Billing; no new action.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_PROFILE_PAGE="false"

# FRONTEND-2 deck-mutation dedupe (needs NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_DECK_MUTATION_REFRESH_ENABLED "true"). Exact "true" enables it; default off, and then a
# deck_mutation commits its count as before. READ AT BUILD TIME: set it on Vercel, then redeploy. On: the slide count a Director deck_mutation commits is
# the one Layout's slide inventory reports (the read the rail list already uses), so a chat add-slide that slide_ready already counted is not counted a
# second time (the rail header and the footer said 7 while the rail list and the canvas said 6). If Layout cannot answer within 4 s, the count from the
# frame stands, as today. Count only: no new message, send payload, cache or history change.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_DECK_MUTATION_DEDUPE="false"
# PASS3 LIBRARY MANAGE (FRONTEND-2, track 4 "more workflows per section"; the Themes and Templates libraries, /studio/themes and /studio/templates; Studio shell only). Two flags, each exact "true",
# default off, and then both libraries are exactly as before. READ AT BUILD TIME: set them on Vercel, then redeploy. Nothing new is needed from the backend: both use Director routes that already exist.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_THEME_LIBRARY_MANAGE: each of the person's own saved themes gets a ⋮ menu ("Manage <name>", like the Decks list) with Rename and Delete. Rename is inline (Enter saves, Esc cancels;
# empty, over 150 characters and a name another theme already has, ignoring case, are refused in the field) and optimistic: the new name shows at once and the old one comes back, with a
# message, if Director does not confirm (PATCH /api/themes/{id} with { name } only). Delete asks first in Studio's own dialog and the theme leaves the list only when Director confirms
# (DELETE /api/themes/{id}); a failure keeps it and shows a message. Decks already built with a theme keep their look (a build copies the theme into the session; no deck points at the saved
# theme), and deleting the standard theme means new presentations use the session default; the dialog says both.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_TEMPLATE_LIBRARY_MANAGE: each of the person's own saved templates gets a ⋮ menu with Delete (DELETE /api/templates/{id}), same dialog and same failure handling. There is NO
# Rename for a template: Director has no template rename route (only PATCH .../blueprint), so the menu holds Delete alone until it has one. Decks already built from a template are not
# changed; a Studio session still rebuilding from it cannot continue with it. A Composer template (an imported deck the Composer library holds) shows Delete disabled with "Composer templates can't be
# deleted here yet.": Director's DELETE would leave its carrier and use records behind. A row Director ever marks as built in or owned by Deckster gets no menu (today Director lists only the person's own).
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_THEME_LIBRARY_MANAGE="false"
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_TEMPLATE_LIBRARY_MANAGE="false"
# STUDIO KG ASK, "Ask your second brain" (FRONTEND-2, the Second Brain page, Pass 3): only the exact value "true" turns it on; default off, and then the page is exactly as before AND the route below answers 404.
# Requires the Studio shell (NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_V4_SHELL "true"). READ AT BUILD TIME: set it on Vercel, then redeploy. On, a question box above the map sends the question to POST /api/knowledge-graph/query
# (a proxy to the Researcher's POST /api/v1/kg/query, same entitlement gate, KNOWLEDGE_SERVICE_URL and KNOWLEDGE_API_KEY as the other /api/knowledge-graph/* routes; the user_id sent is always the signed-in
# person's own) and shows the PASSAGES the person's graph holds on it, each with where it came from (the source link, the deck it was learned in), the related ideas and how they connect. It is not a written
# answer: the Researcher returns a retrieval context pack (entities, relations, cited passages), and there is no LLM answer step. The Researcher needs RESEARCHER_KG_ENABLED and RESEARCHER_KG_RETRIEVAL_ENABLED
# on; with retrieval off it answers an empty pack, which the page shows as "nothing matches yet". Each question costs one text embedding on the Researcher side (no generation). Read only; nothing is written.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_KG_ASK="false"
# STUDIO DECK IMPORT, "Import a PowerPoint as an editable deck" (FRONTEND-2, Pass 3; Director half: Director !518, behind DIRECTOR_DECK_IMPORT_ENABLED). The exact value "true" turns it on; default off, and then the
# Decks page is exactly as before AND both routes named below answer 404 before they read a session or call Director. Needs the Studio shell. Read at build time: set it on Vercel, then redeploy. Do not turn it
# on until Director's own flag is on in the same environment (while it is off Director answers 404 for the start, and the dialog says "Deck import is not available right now."). On: an "Import a PowerPoint"
# button above the Decks page opens a dialog. The .pptx goes to Researcher storage (storageOnly, as the template upload does); POST /api/studio-deck-import (a proxy to Director's
# POST /api/template-ingest/stage/import-reference) starts the import; GET /api/studio-deck-import/jobs/{id} (a proxy to .../stage/jobs/{id}, import jobs only) is polled for Director's own stage words,
# slides done, time left, what changed and the speaker-notes line; when it is ready the Builder opens on /builder?session_id=... A PDF is told "PDF import is coming." and a 4:3 deck is refused by Director
# in its own words. Same Director front door as the template upload (COMPOSER_DIRECTOR_URL, COMPOSER_FRONTDOOR_TOKEN): nothing new to set. The routes sign Director's X-Deckster-Entitlement header on the
# server (class W for the start, class R for each read) only when DECKSTER_REST_ENTITLEMENT_HEADER_ENABLED is ALSO "true" (that flag and its secret are documented where they belong, not here); with it off
# the import works while Director enforces nothing. The import calls no AI model.
# Builder (FRONTEND-1, ruling I5a): the Builder's first-run welcome and its welcome stage gain an "Import a PowerPoint" link to /dashboard?import=pptx, which opens the same dialog on the Decks page. An imported deck also gets one
# small note in the Builder's chat column, "This deck keeps the design of your PowerPoint file. Changing the theme and Add Element are not available for imported decks yet." (contract section 3; the Builder's own refusal
# words are unchanged). The note shows when Director marks the deck's adoption (composer_adoption.source "deck_import", sent on every connect, so any device; Director draft !521) and, as the fallback, in the browser that did the
# import. Off, none of it is drawn.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_DECK_IMPORT="false"

# PASS3 REFINE AN ELEMENT FROM CHAT (FRONTEND-2, Studio half; ops/program/pass3/DIRECTOR-2-REFINE-ELEMENT-DESIGN.md): on only for the exact value "true"; default off, and then the chat sends, the socket
# handling and the page are exactly as before. It is read when Studio is built, so change it on Vercel and redeploy. Needs, in the same environment, Director's DIRECTOR_MDC_REFINE_ELEMENT_ENABLED + CHAT_CAP_REFINE_ELEMENT
# (Director !511, narrowed by !512) and Layout's LAYOUT_REQUEST_ELEMENT_REFINE_ENABLED (layout-builder !245); with Layout's off, every refine answers "failed / viewer_unavailable" and Director says so in chat.
# On: every user_message carries client_caps "element_refine1", and, while an element is selected on the canvas, ONE references entry {kind:"element", element_id, element_type, slide_index,
# slide_id, label} (none for a type off Director's list or an id over 128 characters). Director's element_refine_directive is run like the Element panel's Refine (the element's payload from the
# viewer's requestElementRefine, then the same Text Labs refine, swapped in place) and answered with element_directive_result {directive_id, status, element_id, error_code}. Only the 7 types
# TEXT_BOX, METRICS, TABLE, CHART, IMAGE, ICON_LABEL, SHAPE are refined from chat; any other type or a blank placeholder answers "failed / unsupported_type" with no generation.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAT_ELEMENT_REFINE="false"

# PASS3 THEME CHANGE AND EXPORT FROM CHAT (FRONTEND-2, Studio half of Director !513; streams/director2/theme-export/CONTRACT.md): two independent switches, each
# active only when set to the string "true"; both default off, and then chat sends, socket handling and the page behave as before. Build-time values: change them
# on Vercel and redeploy. They pair with Director's DIRECTOR_MDC_THEME_CHANGE_ENABLED and DIRECTOR_MDC_EXPORT_ENABLED (+ CHAT_CAP_CHANGE_THEME / CHAT_CAP_EXPORT).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAT_THEME_CHANGE: each user_message adds client_caps "theme1"; Director's theme_directive {selection: a preset or a #rrggbb brand colour} goes through
# the theme picker's own apply (without the picker's built-deck lock, which a chat request on a built deck passes; a composer template that keeps its theme,
# Template Mode or a running build still refuse it), the deck-theme set_theme, and is answered from that request's theme_sync. THIS WRITES THE DECK'S THEME.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAT_EXPORT: each user_message adds client_caps "export1"; Director's export_directive {format: pdf | pptx} runs the Download menu's own PDF / PowerPoint
# call (its default quality, its enable rule) and answers "done" once that call has started the browser download. Both answer element_directive_result
# {directive_id, status, error_code}; Studio shows no line of its own (Director's fixed line closes the turn).
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAT_THEME_CHANGE="false"
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAT_EXPORT="false"

# PASS3 MODEL CATALOG (FRONTEND-2, the Intelligence page's "Models" section; Studio shell only): the exact value "true" turns it on, anything else leaves it off. Build-time flag: set it on Vercel and redeploy.
# Off, the page and the Studio API are exactly as before (/api/models/catalogue answers 404). On, a docked "Models" bar below the Intelligence page opens a read-only list of the models Deckster can use for
# each kind of work, read through the Studio route /api/models/catalogue from Director's GET /api/v1/models/catalogue (the browser never calls Director or the router, and Studio holds no router key): the
# certified models per group with vendor, capabilities, context window and output size, a Premium badge and a speed class where one is known, "Suggested" on the proposed shortlist, and "Show all models" (paged).
# No prices are shown: Director's catalogue carries none. The static excerpt in the chooser above is unchanged. It needs Director's own flag (DIRECTOR_MODEL_CATALOGUE_PASSTHROUGH_ENABLED) and the router URL and
# key on Director; until they are set (UAT today) Director answers 503 and the section says "The model catalog isn't available yet". It uses DIRECTOR_API_URL, like the other Studio proxies. No new secret.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_MODEL_CATALOG="false"

# STUDIO NARRATION THROUGH THE MODEL ROUTER (FRONTEND-2, BY10; the server-side narration calls only). These three are plain server variables with no public prefix, so they are read as each request arrives and
# changing one needs no rebuild. The switch is NARRATION_VIA_ROUTER: only the string "true" selects the router. While it is "false" (or anything else), drafting a script and rendering speech call OpenRouter with
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY exactly as they always did, MODEL_ROUTER_URL and MODEL_ROUTER_STUDIO_KEY are never read, and nothing about those calls differs. Selected, drafting a slide script, rendering speech and reading
# a render's billed cost go to MODEL_ROUTER_URL (the router's address with no /v1 on the end) using MODEL_ROUTER_STUDIO_KEY (a router key labelled "studio" with proxy scope, minted by the router's owner;
# it is never committed, so the line below stays empty here). The request bodies are the same as before. The calls add X-MR-Service "studio", X-MR-Task (studio.narration_draft or studio.narration_tts) and
# the signed-in person's opaque id, the session id, the deck id and a trace id; an id that is not made of letters, digits and . _ : - is left out, so an e-mail address is never sent. If either router
# variable is empty the calls go straight to OpenRouter and one line in the server log says so. While OPENROUTER_API_KEY is also set, a call goes to OpenRouter instead ONLY when the router cannot be
# reached, refuses the key (401 or 403), or a proxy answers 502, 503 or 504 with no error object. A timeout after the request was sent, a 429 and every other router answer are final, because a second call
# would be a second charge. Retire OPENROUTER_API_KEY only after a clean run with the switch set to "true".
NARRATION_VIA_ROUTER="false"
MODEL_ROUTER_URL=
MODEL_ROUTER_STUDIO_KEY=

# Server-only real-tier webhook mapping. Only exact "true" enables it; default is off.
# Before enabling, configure all six unique base-plan price IDs in the same Stripe mode.
# Max maps to the existing internal tier "premium". No NEXT_PUBLIC_ aliases are read.
# A subscription whose plan cannot be resolved (unknown price, missing or ambiguous price IDs, no item, more than one base plan) is stored as today (tier pro; an update writes no tier) with one warning in the log, and the webhook still answers 200.
STRIPE_REAL_TIER_MAPPING_ENABLED="false"
STRIPE_STARTER_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID="price_your_starter_monthly_price_id"
STRIPE_STARTER_YEARLY_PRICE_ID="price_your_starter_yearly_price_id"
STRIPE_MAX_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID="price_your_max_monthly_price_id"
STRIPE_MAX_YEARLY_PRICE_ID="price_your_max_yearly_price_id"

# P3-4 RESYNC AFTER A RECONNECT (FRONTEND-2, Studio side of P3-4; the Builder only). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then
# nothing changes. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. Works only with NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_DECK_CHANGED_NOTICE "true" (it reuses
# that notice's inventory read and its deck reload). On: when Director's socket reconnects for the same session and deck (not the first
# connection of a page load), the tab reads the deck's slide inventory once (at most once per 10 s; a hidden tab waits for its own visibility
# read) and, if the deck differs from what it shows, reloads the deck itself when the canvas has no unsaved edits, or else shows the calm
# strip "This deck changed while you were reconnecting · Reload deck" so the user decides. An unchanged deck does nothing. No frame, request
# body, endpoint or saved field changes.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_RECONNECT_RESYNC="false"

# TEXT LABS SIGNED REQUESTS (FRONTEND-2, Studio side of ROUTER-2's Text Labs gate; deckster-workspace
# streams/router/pass3/TL-SIGNED-REQUESTS-CONTRACT.md). Three names, all off or empty by default, and then nothing changes:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_TL_SIGNED_REQUESTS (exact "true"; build-time, change it on Vercel and redeploy): the browser asks Studio's server for a
#   short-lived token (kept in memory only) and sends it as X-MR-Identity-Token on Text Labs' two paid routes, POST /api/chat/message and
#   POST /api/infographic/generate. A 401 the gate gives for a missing / expired / invalid token is answered by minting once more and
#   sending the same request once more; a 429 waits the seconds Text Labs names (at most 30) and sends once more; anything left is
#   shown to the user and not retried automatically. Off: the plain request, no mint call, no header.
# TEXT_LABS_SIGNED_REQUESTS_ENABLED (exact "true"; server-only, read per request): GET /api/identity/text-labs-token mints the token
#   for the signed-in user (540 s). Off: it answers {"token_enabled": false} and issues nothing.
# TEXT_LABS_IDENTITY_SECRET (server-only, a secret: never NEXT_PUBLIC_*): the HMAC key. It must hold exactly the same value as Text Labs'
#   TL_ROUTER_IDENTITY_SECRET, at least 32 random bytes, and differ from DIRECTOR_WS_AUTH_SECRET and RESEARCHER_SESSION_TOKEN_SECRET.
# Flip order: Studio's two switches first; confirm Text Labs logs no 401s; only then Text Labs' TL_REQUIRE_SIGNED_REQUESTS.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_TL_SIGNED_REQUESTS="false"
TEXT_LABS_SIGNED_REQUESTS_ENABLED="false"
TEXT_LABS_IDENTITY_SECRET=

# P3-4 EVERY LONG STUDIO REQUEST ENDS (FRONTEND-2, Studio side of P3-4, slice B). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then
# nothing changes and nothing extra is loaded. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. On, these requests, which could hang
# with a spinner and no end, are aborted at a deadline and end in the failure state they already have (the user runs them again; nothing
# is retried automatically): the PowerPoint export (30 s + 3 s per slide, at most 5 min: derived from the logged 42.7 s for a 42-slide
# PDF, 3x margin), the PDF export (the same rule; the Download menu passes no slide count, so 5 min there), narration script and render
# (315 s: their routes run at most 300 s) and reading or saving the narration voice (30 s). Director's own jobs (slide compose / refine,
# deck build, chat directives) are not timed here: Director's job ledger fails those itself.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_JOB_DEADLINES="false"

# P3-4 DIRECTOR'S JOB LEDGER IN STUDIO (FRONTEND-2, Studio side of P3-4, slice C; the Builder in the Studio shell only). On for the exact value
# "true"; default off, and then nothing changes: Director's job_update frames are dropped as before and nothing is sent. Build-time value:
# change it on Vercel and redeploy. It pairs with Director's DIRECTOR_JOB_LEDGER_ENABLED (!527): with that off no job rows arrive and no card
# shows. On: Director's job rows (job_update frames, and the jobs list of sync_response) are kept per job (the highest seq; a finished row never
# changes), and each slide compose or refine, chat element, refine-element, theme or export directive, or deck build of this session that
# failed or timed out gets one calm card at the end of the chat, in Studio's own words (never the raw error). Retry, only where Director offers
# a frame retry (never for a build, whose text points at Resume, and never for Studio's own REST compose or refine jobs, which keep the rail
# card's retry), sends {"type": "job_retry", "data": {"job_id": "<id>"}} once per click and stays disabled until Director answers or 15 s pass;
# nothing is ever retried automatically. Dismiss hides that card in this tab only and sends nothing. No other frame, request body, endpoint or
# saved field changes.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_JOB_LEDGER="false"

# NEW-DECK HANDOFF SEND (FRONTEND-2, the Builder; Director's new_session directive, MDC P4 / K3). On for the exact value "true"; default
# off, and then nothing changes. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. It matters only with NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAT_DIRECTIVES on
# (Director sends session_directive only to mdc1 clients). On: when Director's new_session directive carries auto_send, Studio opens the
# fresh session, shows the brief as the user's message and sends it there exactly once, as an ordinary user_message with the usual
# client_caps, right after the NEW session's socket opens; a reconnect, a socket that drops and opens again, or a retry never sends it a
# second time. If that socket does not open within 12 s, nothing is sent and nothing is retried: the message is taken away, the brief goes
# back in the input box and the usual "Couldn't reach the Director" notice shows, so the user sends it. Off: the old path, whose send still
# waited on the old session's socket and so never went out. A directive without auto_send only fills the input box, on or off.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_NEW_DECK_HANDOFF_SEND="false"

# PUBLISH REVIEW FIT (FRONTEND-2, the Builder's Publish dialog; the setup wizard on a phone). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then
# nothing changes. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. It matters only with NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_POLISH on (the rule it fixes is that
# change's). On: at phone width (700 px and below) the setup wizard's step body no longer pokes 4 px past the edge of its scrolling grid, so the Review
# step stops scrolling sideways and its right-hand tiles keep their edge; the content does not move. Wider windows and every other dialog are unchanged.
# Off: the dialog is as before.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_PUBLISH_REVIEW_FIT="false"

# VERSION HISTORY, DECK ONLY (FRONTEND-2, the Builder's profile menu; design #456). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then
# nothing changes. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. It matters only with NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_VERSION_HISTORY_V2 on. On: the
# menu's "Version history" row is there only while a deck is on stage. On a new session the welcome is on stage with a blank deck behind it, so
# the row showed on the empty Builder and, when chosen, did nothing; with this on it is gone until a deck is on stage (a generated or
# authored deck, or the blank canvas once it is chosen). A session that has a deck, and every other page, is unchanged. Off: the row shows
# as before.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_VERSION_HISTORY_DECK_ONLY="false"

# ADD SLIDE COMPOSE SIGNS ITS USER (FRONTEND-2, stacked on #475; the Next proxy POST /api/slides/compose only). A plain SERVER variable (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, no rebuild): it is read as each request
# arrives, and only the exact value "true" turns it on; default off, and then the request to Director is byte-for-byte what it was. It pairs with Director !535 (DIRECTOR_ROUTER_COMPOSE_BIND_USER_ENABLED,
# off): Director binds a compose to its user for Model Router attribution ONLY when the request carries a verified X-Deckster-Entitlement (typ "rest", m "POST", sub equal to the body's user_id) AND that id is
# a valid router id as it stands. On, Studio adds that header (signed per request, on the server, by the same helper the deck-import routes use) ONLY when the body's user_id is the person's canonical id
# (the session user's id, or the Knowledge-Graph gate's id on that branch; never the e-mail the route falls back to when a session has no id) and that id matches Director's clean_id rule: starts with a
# letter or digit, then letters, digits and . _ : -, at most 255 characters, ASCII only (director-v4.0 src/utils/mr_context.py:84,101-111). Any other case adds no header and changes nothing. The body's
# user_id is chosen exactly as before. It also needs DECKSTER_REST_ENTITLEMENT_HEADER_ENABLED "true" and DIRECTOR_WS_AUTH_SECRET (the shared helper's own rules; documented where they belong, not here).
# Flip order: either side first is safe (Director ignores a header it does not know; Studio's header alone binds nothing); the bind needs both.
STUDIO_COMPOSE_ENTITLEMENT_ENABLED="false"

# PUBLISH PREVIEW FROM LAYOUT'S INVENTORY (FRONTEND-2, the Publish dialog's "What viewers get"; THUMBNAILS-BLANK-UAT fix 1). On for the exact value "true"; default
# off, and then nothing changes: no inventory read and the same preview as before. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. On: when the preview has neither
# a live Stage F image from this tab nor a restored thumbnail (thumbnail_url with a matching thumbnail_presentation_id), which is any deck not built in this tab, Studio
# reads the Final deck's slide inventory ONCE (GET {layout}/api/presentations/{id}/slides/inventory, the rail's own reader and Layout URL) and shows slide 1's
# thumbnail_url only when it is fresh: not null, not thumbnail_stale, and from this presentation's own inventory. Stale or none: "Deck preview unavailable", as before.
# While the read is in flight the existing "Loading deck preview..." state shows; a failed read shows the unavailable state. A live or restored image always wins and
# makes no read.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_PUBLISH_PREVIEW_INVENTORY_ENABLED="false"

# PAYMENTS OPEN SOON (FRONTEND-2, controlled release; there is no Stripe account yet). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then nothing changes.
# Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. On: every control that would start a NEW payment is disabled and says "Payments open soon": Billing's
# "Upgrade Now", "Upgrade to <plan>", "View Plans" and the four credit-pack buttons, the account menu's "Upgrade for more usage" row, and the Builder's reserve-credit
# top-up buttons. The two checkout routes (POST /api/stripe/create-checkout-session and /api/stripe/create-topup-session) answer 503 {"error":"Payments open soon"}
# before the session, the Stripe customer or Stripe is touched, so a page that was open before the deploy cannot start a payment either. Left exactly as they are: the plan a
# user is on (name, price, status, renewal; a Pro or Max subscriber sees what they saw), "Manage Subscription" (the Stripe portal link of an existing subscriber), the
# credit balance and its transactions, invites, coupons and their redemption, and the Stripe real-tier flag and its code path.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_PAYMENTS_OPEN_SOON="false"

# DUPLICATE COPY TITLE (FRONTEND-2; follows the Decks page's "Duplicate" item). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then nothing changes. Build-time value: change it on
# Vercel and redeploy. It matters only for a deck that was copied. On: (1) on the Decks page a copy's card keeps its " (copy)" suffix visible: the original and its copy both cut to the same words
# ("moving weekly status meeting..."), so the name is cut with an ellipsis BEFORE the suffix, the suffix never shrinks, and the card's link says the full name as its tooltip; (2) the copy's Builder
# header shows the copy's own title (the session's stored title, found through the copy's "copied from" marker) instead of "Studio", which is what a deck with no slide structure of its own showed.
# Nothing is written and no request body changes: the Builder reads the one open session once (the read the copy's "Copied from" note already makes), and only while its header has no title of its own.
# A deck that was not copied is drawn exactly as before, on the Decks page and in the Builder.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_DUPLICATE_COPY_TITLE="false"

# THUMBNAIL LAST GOOD (FRONTEND-2, THUMBNAILS-BLANK-UAT "never blank"; the Studio half of Layout's LAYOUT_THUMBNAIL_LAST_GOOD_ENABLED). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then nothing changes: every rail card and the Publish
# preview are exactly as before. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. Layout adds two keys to each row of GET /api/presentations/{id}/slides/inventory: last_good_thumbnail_url (the slide's last registered preview, fresh or
# stale) and thumbnail_stale_reason ("content" or "theme"); with Layout's flag off both are absent and read as null here. On: (1) the slide rail, which needs NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_RAIL_SLIDE_IDENTITY_ENABLED to read the inventory, shows a slide
# with no fresh preview as ITS OWN last good image (never another slide's) with a small "May lag" badge and the label "Preview may not show recent edits" (the slide changed since the capture; also the label for no reason or an unknown one) or
# "Preview shows the previous theme" (the deck's theme changed); a fresh preview shows alone, as before, and a slide with no image at all keeps the loading or "No preview" card; (2) the Publish preview, ONLY when
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_PUBLISH_PREVIEW_INVENTORY_ENABLED is on too, falls back to slide 1's last good image when it has no fresh one, so "Deck preview unavailable" shows only when no image exists at all (its caption already says "Preview image can
# lag recent edits"); with only that flag on, the Publish preview still shows a fresh image only. No new request is made and nothing is written.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_THUMBNAIL_LAST_GOOD="false"

# STUDIO BULK EDIT + CHAT UNDO (FRONTEND-2, PROGRAM-1 SUPERCHARGE I2; the Studio side of DIRECTOR-2's whole-deck edits and chat undo). Two flags, each on only for the exact value "true"; default off, and then nothing changes: no cap is
# sent, no frame is looked at and every chat line and ask is drawn exactly as before. Build-time values: change them on Vercel and redeploy. Director needs its own flags on, and sends these frames ONLY to a client whose user_message advertised
# bulk_edit1 / undo1 (Studio does that only with its flag on), so the frame itself is the capability: it is drawn when it arrives, with or without a sync_response (a brand-new session never gets one). Both are drawn in the Studio shell only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_BULK_EDIT: every send also carries client_caps "bulk_edit1" (after the other caps). A whole-deck edit ("shorten every title") arrives as an ask (action_request, kind "bulk_edit_confirm") and is drawn as a card: your
# instruction, "N slides", a chip per slide (its number, and its title when the deck's structure names it), Director's own estimate label (never a figure Studio works out), and Director's two answers ("Change N slides" and "Cancel"). The
# answer is sent like any other ask: one user_message whose data.action_value is that action's value (confirm_bulk_edit:<bulk_id> or cancel_bulk_edit:<bulk_id>). One answer only; then both buttons are disabled and the chosen one is marked.
# Then bulk_edit_progress receipts show on the chips as they arrive (changed, couldn't change with Director's reason, skipped) and bulk_edit_summary shows counts ("4 of 6 changed · 2 failed"), never "all changed" unless every slide changed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_UNDO: every send also carries client_caps "undo1". Director's change_recorded (for the displayed deck only) puts a small "Undo" chip under the Director chat line that reported the change. One click sends ONE
# user_message with data.action_value "undo_change:<change_id>"; Studio never writes to Layout. Only the latest change can be undone: a newer change_recorded turns the older chips into "A later change replaced this". The reply
# (undo_result) ends the chip as "Undone", "Couldn't undo: <reason>" or "A later change replaced this". Director's deck_mutation {mutation:"deck_restored"} is read, with this flag on, as a whole-viewer refresh (the hook treats it as slide_replaced
# with the slide count left to the rail's re-read); it is acted on only when NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_DECK_MUTATION_REFRESH_ENABLED is on too (that flag owns the viewer reload), and is ignored with this flag off. Receipts, summaries and chips are kept in
# this tab's memory only: a reload shows Director's chat lines, not them.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_BULK_EDIT="false"
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_UNDO="false"

# PASS2 ADMIN (FRONTEND-1, the internal /admin/users and /admin/coupons pages): an exact "true" turns it on; default off, and then both pages are exactly as before. READ AT BUILD TIME: set it on Vercel, then
# redeploy. It needs no other flag: the pages sit outside the Studio shell, so on they draw its palette, type and spacing themselves, light and dark (the old header stayed white in dark mode, and its badge was
# unreadable). On, the same six requests with the same bodies, the same sign-in redirect and the same "Access denied" for a 403 (who may open them is still decided only by app/api/admin: nothing here is a
# permission rule). What changes: a failed read is no longer "Access denied" and a redirect (users) or a spinner that never ends (coupons) but "could not be loaded" with Try again; a failed Approve / Revoke /
# Enable / Disable / Create / Copy says so; a refresh keeps the page in place; both pages link to each other and to Studio; "premium" reads "Max" on both; an expired coupon says "Expired"; the search ignores
# spaces around it; a missing or invalid date cannot blank the page. Nothing is added that an admin could not do before.
# HARDENING (same flag, PROGRAM-1 ruling 22 Oct): on, /admin/* is also guarded in middleware.ts (nobody signed in goes to sign-in and comes back; a signed-in account that is not the admin goes to /builder, where the
# pages sent it after a 403; the API routes keep their own checks and who is admin is unchanged: the email in DEV_BYPASS_EMAIL); GET and POST /api/admin/coupons (and PATCH /api/admin/coupons/[id]) answer 401, not
# 403, when nobody is signed in; the users and coupons lists are read a page at a time (25 rows, at most 100; the users read also takes filter and q, so its figures cover everyone); a new coupon's expiry is sent with
# the admin's time zone offset (2026-12-31T23:59:00-05:00) and the routes refuse one without a zone. Stored data: only a coupon created or changed with the flag on reads its expiry in the admin's zone; before, the bare
# wall time was read in the server's zone (UTC on Vercel), and rows already stored are not touched.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_ADMIN="false"

# PASS2 Docs / Help / Legal / Agents (FRONTEND-1, the public pages /docs, /docs/<category>/<article>, /docs/api, /legal/{privacy,terms,security,cookies}, /agents/<agent> and, in the Studio shell, /help; there is no mockup for any
# of them): exact "true" turns it on; default off, and then every page is exactly as before. READ AT BUILD TIME: set it on Vercel, then redeploy. The public pages keep the site's own header and footer and take the Studio shell's
# tokens (light and dark) and type scale; /help is already inside the Studio shell (NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_V4_SHELL "true") and without the shell stays untouched. On: /docs and each article are rebuilt (a card's line of text is the
# article's first paragraph, not its raw markdown; the side list names only the articles that exist, the old one linked three that do not; the article's title is its page heading once, not twice; no dead "Share" button;
# a search with no hit says so; the article list is reachable on a phone; a link into the docs that goes nowhere is plain text); the legal, API and agent pages keep their words and links and change only their look (no
# purple-to-blue gradients, one accent, the shell's type, readable in dark, the dark wordmark lifted); /help keeps its layout and gets the finishing touches (the header's label on its centre line and off the window's edge, one
# type scale for the step, agent and tip lines, "Start Creating" in the ink action colour, a framed empty search). Every page's browser tab names it (Privacy Policy, Terms of Service, Documentation, each article, each agent), and
# the three titles that read "... | Deckster | Deckster" (API Documentation, Cookie Policy, Security & Compliance) read "... | Deckster" (Help Center has the same fault, but app/help/layout.tsx is pinned byte for byte by
# scripts/test-atlas-help-recovery.mjs, so it is left). /integrations and /agents are redirects (next.config.mjs), so those two pages are not touched. No new action.
# Content pass (PROGRAM-1, 22 Oct), same flag: the docs text names the current eight agents (Director, Researcher, Analyst, Content Generator, Visualizer, Theme Builder, Slide Composer, Element Generator) instead of Scripter, Graphic Artist
# and Data Visualizer (content/docs.ts is not edited; content/studio-p2-docs-agents.ts swaps the text when the flag is on); /docs/api says "Not available yet" in a notice under the site header with its content muted, and no footer links to
# it; neither footer links /integrations or /agents, and /compare drops "Meet the Team" (it pointed at /agents); the Landing footer gains Help, Docs, Security and Cookies beside Privacy and Terms. The words of the legal pages are not touched.
# Content pass 2 (PROGRAM-1, 22 Oct), same flag: the docs name the real plans (Starter, Pro, Max; the plan tags the code does not back are taken out) and the Google sign-in (content/studio-p2-docs-facts.ts); the comparison pages and the example and template
# cards read the current agents (content/studio-p2-comparisons.ts, lib/studio-p2-docs.ts; /examples and /templates are redirects today); /docs/api loses its "v1.0 Beta" badge; the agent not-found page links to /experts. With NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_ONBOARDING
# and the shell on there is no old agent name left to change (the wizard and the Studio introduction name none); the old /onboarding page and the old modal, which still do, are the flag-off text and stay as they were.
# Content pass 3 (PROGRAM-1, 22 Oct), same flag: /docs/api loses its Rate Limits section, the heading with its lock icon and the line ("100 requests per minute for Pro plans and 1000 requests per minute for Enterprise plans": the API is not open and no plan is called
# Enterprise); the rest of the page is as it was.
# Content pass 4 (PROGRAM-1, 23 Oct; Docs ruling 2 is lifted for what `uat` already removed, so this supersedes "The words of the legal pages are not touched." above for the Security page only), same flag: the Security page and its tab description say
# only what is true today (content/studio-p2-docs-security.ts, the wording `uat` already carries): no SOC 2 Type II, GDPR, AWS, audit, multi-factor or security@ claim; the footer drops its "GDPR Compliant" and "99.9% Uptime" lines (SSL Encrypted and
# Privacy First stay). The words of the Privacy, Terms and Cookies pages are not touched.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_DOCS="false"

# STUDIO NEW LOGO (FRONTEND-1, Pass 3, PROGRAM-1 ask 3): the tile at the top left of the Studio rail (the Builder, the library pages, Help and the session-problem view) shows the new Deckster logo mark (public/logo-icon-sm.png,
# the L-B mark the sign-in pages and the account header already use) instead of the purple square holding a Layers icon. Set it to the string true to turn it on; any other value, or none, leaves the tile exactly as before.
# The value is baked into the bundle when Vercel builds, so change it there and redeploy. It matters only inside the Studio shell (NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_V4_SHELL), because the rail exists only there. The tile keeps its link (home), its name ("Deckster home"), its tooltip and its 32px box.
# The logo and app icon FILES are not behind this flag (they ship with the UAT marketing port's commit, same names and sizes); this flag only puts the logo where the rail had an icon.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_NEW_LOGO="false"

# UAT MARKETING PORT (FRONTEND-1, Pass 3): the seven Landing pages (/, /bring, /present, /experts, /pricing, /about, /learn) take the UAT design of 3-4 Oct 2026 (status pills from one config, "Request access" CTAs, the hero film, gallery wall,
# the L-B logo mark, UAT's own phone menu, per-page share cards, /sitemap.xml). Only the value true turns it on; anything else is off, and then every page is exactly as before. READ AT BUILD TIME: set it on Vercel, then redeploy.
# It lives in a parallel tree (components/marketing/v3-uat, lib/marketing/v3-uat-content.ts, styles/marketing-v3-uat.css, public/marketing/v3-uat), so nothing of it renders with the flag off. With the Pass 2 Landing flag also on,
# Narration and Viewers-ask read "Live" (the later ruling) and the Pass 2 night background stays; with the Pass 2 Docs flag on the footer keeps its Help / Docs / Security / Cookies links; with the Pass 2 Account flag on the plan words are the shared plan list's.
# NOT behind this flag: the L-B logo and app icon files (same file names and sizes as before, so they cannot be switched; they also replace the broken placeholder PWA icons).
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_UAT_MARKETING="false"

# TEMPLATE RENAME (FRONTEND-1, Pass 3, same flag NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_TEMPLATE_LIBRARY_MANAGE, so it adds no flag of its own; this block supersedes the sentence above that says a template has no Rename): the ⋮ menu of each of the person's own saved
# templates also gets Rename, inline like a theme's (Enter saves, Esc cancels; empty, over 150 characters and a name another template already has, ignoring case, are refused in the field; optimistic, the old name comes back with a message
# if Director does not confirm). A Composer template renames too: only its name changes (Delete stays disabled for it). Studio calls PATCH /api/templates/{id} with { name } only, which forwards to Director's PATCH /api/users/{uid}/templates/{id};
# that route sits behind DIRECTOR_TEMPLATE_RENAME_ENABLED on the Director (default off, and it then answers 405). While it is off the first Rename attempt is refused, the old name comes back, and Rename shows disabled with "Renaming templates isn't
# available yet." until the page is reloaded. A Director 409 (a name the person already has) or 422 (a refused name) is shown under the name field; a 404 "template not found" says the template is no longer available.

# PASS3 LAUNCHED WORDING (FRONTEND-1, PK 23 Oct "replace 'coming soon' / mock wording with launched wording, grey out what is not ready"): the string "true" turns it on; any other value or none, and every page is exactly as before.
# READ AT BUILD TIME: set it on Vercel, then redeploy. Studio pages only (the marketing, legal and docs trees are not touched). On: a sentence that promised a later release or named a developer concept now says what is true today
# (Settings > Security "Planned" two-factor row is "Via Google"; Privacy "Planned" profile visibility is "Private"; the three notification switches are disabled and read off, because nothing sends those emails; Help answers that
# named a notification or told people to browse ready-made templates are corrected, and the share answer names Publish; "Outline previews" replaces the "Coming soon" card on the old Decks page, and the Folders chips (every deck is in
# "general") are not drawn; the Decks menu note for Duplicate says it is not available right now; Intelligence says choices do not change which models Deckster uses, "Your own intelligence" is a disabled "Not available" button, and the
# model catalog notice no longer says it will appear; Your details loses "optional later additions"; PDF import and follow-up questions no longer say they are coming; the template library and theme workspace notices drop "enabled",
# "environment" and "connected"; /shortcuts lists only the shortcuts that have a handler even without NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_P2_ACCOUNT; the pending-approval page drops the 24-48 hour and email promise; the sign-up benefits say
# "Reusable templates from your own decks" and "Your account is approved by our team before first use"; the disabled Template button's tooltip, the builder's templates-off notice and the Export tooltip before a deck is ready lose "coming soon",
# "environment" and "Stage 4"). Paths that need real work to reword (the old Intelligence prototype view, the old onboarding modal and page, the old billing plan list, the Duplicate-deck, template-progress and Add Slide blocker sentences that
# come from the pure word files) are left as they were. No new action, no request, no stored value.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_LAUNCH_WORDING="false"

# STUDIO FIRST PAINT (COMPOSER-2, FUTURE-OPS-2 section 3 row 4). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then nothing changes: no connection is
# opened early and the viewer polls exactly as before. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. On: (1) the viewer asks React 19 to open connections early (preconnect and dns-prefetch links, hoisted into <head>) to the Layout service
# (NEXT_PUBLIC_LAYOUT_SERVICE_URL) and to the four hosts Layout's viewer page loads from: cdn.jsdelivr.net, cdn.tailwindcss.com, fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com (the last one cross-origin, as fonts are); (2) the viewer's slide-info poll,
# which sends getCurrentSlideInfo (composeGetState while a compose job runs) to the Layout frame every 3 s and so waited 3 s after the frame loaded, also sends ONE at once when it starts for a frame that has just loaded. That first poll is a head start:
# when it gets no usable answer (the frame's scripts are not ready, a timeout, an error) it counts nothing against the polling backoff, and the interval ticks are the same as before; while it is in flight the interval ticks wait, so two polls never
# overlap. No new request type, no write, no change to a request body.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_FIRST_PAINT_ENABLED="false"

# DECK CARD THUMBNAILS (COMPOSER-2, the Decks page's deck cards; PROGRAM-1 "thumbnails instead of live viewers in the deck list"). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and
# then nothing changes: every card is the live viewer frame as before and no inventory read is made. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. On: a card whose viewer URL is
# allowed (and on the configured Layout) shows its deck's first-slide image instead of the viewer. ONE read per deck, on the card's first visibility and never while it is off-screen, of
# Layout's slide inventory (GET {layout}/api/presentations/{id}/slides/inventory, the rail's own route): slide 1's thumbnail_url, else last_good_thumbnail_url (additive; absent unless
# Layout's LAYOUT_THUMBNAIL_LAST_GOOD_ENABLED is on) with a small "May lag" cue. A failed or slow read (8 s), a row without an image, or an image that does not load keeps today's card.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_DECK_CARD_THUMBNAILS_ENABLED="false"

# STUDIO PASS 3 POLISH (FRONTEND-2, PROGRAM-1 Saturday evening push, 24 Oct: a polish sweep of every Studio page at phone and desktop width; ONE flag for the whole set). On for the exact value
# "true"; default off, and then nothing changes: no attribute is set, no rule matches, and no markup, handler, request or stored value differs. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy.
# Needs the Studio shell (NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_V4_SHELL). On: <html> carries data-studio-pass3-polish="true" while a Studio route is on screen (the account layout and the Builder set it, and it comes
# off when the route goes), and one stylesheet, every rule scoped to that attribute, applies. PR A has five sections. (1) Decks and Knowledge on a phone (640 px and below): the 64 px right gutter
# becomes 16 px (the page's own) and the Replay-intro button, fixed in the viewport corner, sits in the flow at the end of the page, right-aligned; the 52 px of bottom padding that reserved its
# corner goes back to 28 px. (2) iOS focus zoom (640 px and below): text inputs, native selects, textareas and contenteditable are 16 px (the Director prompt was 13.6 px, the Decks search 13 px, the
# composer menus 11.5 px), with line height 1.5 on textareas and 1.35 on inputs; padding, height, width, buttons, labels and icons are not touched, and Settings and profile pages, Billing,
# Shortcuts, Your details, the account menu, Publish, the published viewer, Admin, Docs and Help are kept out. (3) The Builder root (h-screen, which is 100vh) is 100dvh where the browser has dvh, so
# on a phone the composer is not under the browser toolbar; on a desktop browser dvh and vh are the same. (4) Phone tap targets (640 px and below, Studio shell only): the Builder header's panel
# toggle (27 px), New deck (28 px tall) and Export (28 px tall), the composer toolbar's buttons (28 px) and the Replay-intro button (28 to 30 px) get a 32 px minimum width and height, content
# centred, icons and type unchanged; the Slides / Director segments keep their 22 px box and get a 32 px hit area from an ::after extension. (5) More phone tap targets (640 px and below): the Decks
# Grid / List toggle (28 px tall) and, on Templates and Themes, the "Start another draft" button (27 px), "Back to Studio" (30.5 px) and the disclosure summaries (22.5 px; 8 px of padding above and
# below) get a 32 px minimum height. Later PRs add numbered sections to the same stylesheet under the same flag.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_PASS3_POLISH="false"

# STUDIO BULK EDIT PROMPT TEXT (FRONTEND-2; follows the whole-deck edit card, NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_BULK_EDIT). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then nothing changes: the card is drawn exactly as before.
# Flip it TOGETHER with Director's DIRECTOR_MDC_BULK_EDIT_POLISH_ENABLED: Director's polished confirm sends its own sentence for the card (payload.prompt_text: what it will change, how, and the rough cost), and with
# this flag on the card draws that sentence once, as plain text, under the "Whole-deck change" heading and before the quoted instruction. The sentence already carries the estimate label, so the card's own
# "Estimate:" line is then left out (the label is never drawn twice); a missing or empty sentence draws nothing new. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. Safe to set before the Director flag: no sentence, no change.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_BULK_EDIT_PROMPT_TEXT="false"

# STUDIO LEGAL SHORT LINKS (FRONTEND-2; PROGRAM-1 decision D16 a, 25 Oct). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then /terms and /privacy are the not-found page, as before. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy.
# On: /terms redirects to /legal/terms and /privacy to /legal/privacy (HTTP 307, the same as the two non-permanent redirects in `uat`'s next.config.mjs, which the Studio tree's next.config.mjs does not carry). Sign-in and sign-up, links outside
# the app and the Google sign-in consent screen use the short paths; the request's own query string is carried to the legal page. Set it to "true" on UAT and on production for parity with `uat`. Not behind this flag: the marketing-slide
# cache header (Cache-Control public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800 on /marketing/v3/slides/* and on /marketing/v3-uat/slides/*, the stills the UAT marketing copy serves) is two entries in vercel.json, and a
# deploy config file cannot read an environment variable.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_LEGAL_SHORT_LINKS="false"

# STUDIO PHONE SHELL (FRONTEND-2; PK's phone review, 25 Oct, decisions A and B; two stacked PRs, ONE flag). On for the exact value "true" together with NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_V4_SHELL; default off, and then nothing
# changes: no element is drawn and no rule matches. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. Phones only (640 px and narrower) unless said: tablets and desktops keep the rail. PR 1: the left icon rail
# gives way to a bottom tab bar (Studio, Decks, Templates, Themes, More; the current tab in the accent colour, 44 x 48 px targets, above the home indicator's safe area); More is a sheet with Second brain,
# Intelligence, Your details, Help and the account menu; the rail's brand tile (the new logo mark when the new-logo flag is on) stays at the top left of the top bar; pages get bottom padding
# for the bar, and on /builder the bar steps aside while the Director prompt has focus. PR 2: the Builder top is one row (logo, a "..." menu with the deck title, the deck list, New deck, Export, Notes,
# Thumbnails and the slide panel, then Publish) over today's Slides | Director switch, whose Director segment carries a connection dot; the separate "Director / Connected" row and the edge pull tabs go.
# On desktop (PR 2) the Director panel's status line becomes a dot beside "Director", with words only when it is not connected.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_PHONE_SHELL="false"

# STUDIO SPEED PERCEIVED (FRONTEND-2; SPEED + ROUTER ACCELERATION, 25 Oct). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then the chat and the composer get exactly the props they get today. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy.
# On: a message typed in the composer shows in the chat at once as a quiet "Sending…" echo while the first save of a new deck (the session row, and the blank-canvas check with Layout when there is one: 0.5-1.6 s today)
# and a reconnect in flight finish; a socket already closed before Enter is refused in both builds (the existing "Reconnecting" toast keeps the draft). The page still sends, commits and persists exactly as before: the echo leaves
# in the render where the real bubble appears. A send that settles within 80 ms never shows one. When a send fails (the existing toast says why and keeps the draft), the echo reads "Not sent. Your message is still in the box."
# until the draft changes or 6 s pass. No Director change.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_SPEED_PERCEIVED="false"

# STUDIO FLOW FOCUS (FRONTEND-1; P3-1 D "flow control", Studio half). On only for the string "true"; default off, and then nothing changes: no listener, no timer, no navigation. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy.
# On: when Director changes or builds a slide of the deck on the stage (a deck_mutation, a change_recorded that names a slide, a partial slide_update, a slide_built or a slide_ready), the stage goes to that slide: the new position of a moved slide, 0-based on the wire
# except slide_update, which counts from 1 and is converted. On a narrow layout (one pane at a time) the stage pane is brought up first; a restored deck only brings the stage up. Frames for another deck, a deleted slide and build_event / slide_progress (they carry
# no presentation id) are ignored. Not for 4 s after the user navigated by hand (a pane switch, a rail click, a slide change in the viewer), and during a build only while the user has not navigated at all: the follow is of the newest built slide, once. Safe to set before any Director change.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_FLOW_FOCUS="false"
# STUDIO FLOW AMEND (FRONTEND-1; P3-1 D). On only for the string "true" AND only together with NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILD_NARRATION and NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILD_CONTROL; default off, and then the chat and the composer are exactly as before. Build-time value.
# On: while a build is paused or stopped the composer can send (the reply gate that waits for Director is released, as Esc does), a calm line sits above it ("Paused - type changes, then Resume or Rebuild."), and two buttons: Resume, and "Rebuild with these instructions"
# (stop, wait for Director's build_phase "settled" for up to 8 s, then send the typed text as an ordinary message; the line says "Rebuilding once the last slide finishes" meanwhile). Director's build_phase "settled" is read here and never reaches the narration, so set this
# flag BEFORE Director's DIRECTOR_FLOW_STEER_ENABLED. A message sent while paused is queued by Director (build_phase paused, steer_pending): the line then says "Changes queued for resume."
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_FLOW_AMEND="false"
# STUDIO FLOW AMEND INSTRUCTIONS (FRONTEND-1; P3-1 D). On only for the string "true" together with the amend flag above; default off. Build-time value. On: Resume with typed text sends it in build_control {action: "resume", instructions} (cut to Director's 1000 characters), clears the box,
# and shows "Applied to slides N-M." when Director's building acknowledgement names the slides (applied_to). When applied_to is empty (the slides are already in progress) it says so plainly, puts the text back in the box and offers Rebuild.
# Leave it off until Director ships the field (DIRECTOR_FLOW_STEER_ENABLED): today nothing accepts it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_FLOW_AMEND_INSTRUCTIONS="false"

# STUDIO ARRANGE (FRONTEND-2, 26 Oct; pairs with Layout !260, LAYOUT_ARRANGE_COMMANDS_ENABLED: both flip together). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then selection and the Format inspector behave exactly as today.
# Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy.
# On: selecting an element no longer raises it (the viewer sent bringToFront on every selection, which Layout's flag turns into a saved raise); ordering happens only through Arrange or chat.
# The v4 Format inspector's Arrange tab works: Order, Align to slide, Position and Size in slide pixels of the 1920 x 1080 slide (Layout snaps to its 12 px grid and keeps the element on the slide).
# Lock, Rotate, Flip and style classes show "Not available yet" (Lock until Layout lets a locked element be selected again); an element already locked shows only Unlock; shapes and tables show every Arrange
# control disabled. A refusal from the viewer is shown in plain words.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_ARRANGE="false"

# P3-10 MODEL CHOICE (FRONTEND-2): the Intelligence page's model chooser offers, per text task, the models and presets the live model catalogue opens for it (Fast / Balanced / Best with a cost
# hint), for "Reusable defaults" or "This presentation" (the Builder session). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then the page is exactly as before and the three new server routes
# (/api/model-choice/prefs, /api/model-choice/prefs/deck/{session id}, /api/model-choice/used/{build id}) answer 404. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. The chooser acts only while the Pass 2
# Intelligence flag is "true" too, and reads the catalogue only while the Models section's catalogue flag is on. The routes save choices in the Model Router at the router address the narration block
# above sets, with MODEL_ROUTER_FRONTEND_KEY: server-only, a router key labelled "frontend" with the prefs and read scopes, minted by the router's owner, never sent to the browser or logged.
# While either is empty the routes answer 503 and choices stay in this browser, and the page says so. The page mounts the chooser once its two-line page hook lands (held for PK's OK on three pins).
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_MODEL_CHOICE="false"
MODEL_ROUTER_FRONTEND_KEY=

# STUDIO CHAT CLEAN (FRONTEND-1; P3-1 C "chat clean v3", PK's design of 26 Oct, composer per v3.1). On only for the string "true"; default off, and then the Director chat, the build row and the composer are byte for byte what they were. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. Studio shell only.
# On: the Director chat is one quiet thread (streams/frontend1/chat-design/v3): the user's turn is a right-aligned box in the one tinted colour, Director's words sit on the page with no box, label or time, an ask's choices are hairline chips with the chosen one outlined in ink, the header's
# connection dot is green when connected, amber while connecting and grey otherwise, and with NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILD_NARRATION the build is an outlined job card inline at the end of the thread (Plan › Outline › Build › Check › Package, one latest line, the elapsed clock) in place of the
# "Director is working" row, with small notes for each stop and resume. The composer is a hairline box: attach, template and theme as small square buttons, the research options button (deep research / web search / knowledge graph, as today) next to Send with a dot while any is on,
# the model picker as a gauge button (shown only with NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_MODEL_CHOICE), and, with NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILD_CONTROL, Send becomes Stop while a build runs (build_control stop: finished slides are kept); the ribbon's Pause / Stop and the flow bar are not drawn. A stopped build is a
# slim bar above the composer ("Stopped at slide 5 · slides 1–4 kept" with Continue = build_control resume), and the composer stays free: Enter with new directions always sends build_control resume {instructions} (1000 characters at most; Director's building acknowledgement names
# the slides it applied them to, or says nothing was left to build), whatever the NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_FLOW_* flags say (Director: a plain message after a stop is an ordinary chat turn and never rebuilds). No text is drawn larger than the chat draws it today. PK's open choices (the accent,
# the Stop colour, the primary action after a stop, the Director label, the user-box tint, where the research switches live) are one token each in lib/studio-chat-clean.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_CLEAN="false"

# STUDIO CHAT ELEMENT EDIT (FRONTEND-2, P3-1 A chat parity; the Studio side of DIRECTOR-2's DIRECTOR_MDC_ELEMENT_EDIT_ENABLED, contract: streams/director2/element-edit/CONTRACT.md). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then nothing changes: no cap is sent,
# no frame is looked at, and the Notes panel listens for nothing. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. On: every send also carries client_caps "element_edit1" and "notes1" (after mdc1 and the other caps). Director's element_edit
# {payload:{op: delete | order | place | style, ...}} runs through the presentation viewer's own element commands (deleteElement, bringTextBoxToFront / sendTextBoxToBack, resizeTextBox, setTextBoxFontWeight / FontSize / Color / Alignment, and Layout's Arrange commands
# bringToFront / sendToBack / bringForward / sendBackward / alignElement, always with intent "arrange"; those pair with Layout's LAYOUT_ARRANGE_COMMANDS_ENABLED, !260 / !261, and without it the viewer answers "Unknown action" = UNSUPPORTED_OP), never a server PATCH, and is
# answered ONCE with element_edit_result {payload:{directive_id, ok, error_code}}: ok:true only after the viewer's autosave acknowledged the change (Studio enters edit mode the way selecting an element does and flushes with the viewer's own Save). What the viewer cannot do
# (italic, style on anything but a text box, an element type Arrange refuses) is UNSUPPORTED_OP, never faked. A stale socket or owner sends nothing; a second edit while one runs is BUSY. deck_mutation payload.mutation "notes_updated" makes the Notes panel read the deck
# again, so Director's notes show; every other deck_mutation is untouched. No Director change: Director needs its own flag on.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_ELEMENT_EDIT="false"

# STUDIO CHAT COMMANDS (FRONTEND-2; P3-1 A chat parity, PK's ask of 27 Oct). On only for the string "true"; default off, and then the composer, the sends and the socket frames are byte for byte what they were. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. It needs NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_CLEAN and the Studio shell (the menus live in the v3.1 composer); without them it does nothing.
# On: typing "/" at the start of the composer (or after a space) opens a short command menu (type to filter; arrows, Enter or Tab, Esc; 44 px rows on phones): /add-slide, /duplicate and /delete fill in an editable request for the current slide (nothing is sent until Send), /theme, /template and /model open the composer's own pickers,
# /research and /web flip the options menu's switches (the same lock), /export pdf|pptx runs the Download menu's own export, /undo presses the Undo chip, /stop is the Send/Stop control's stop, and /publish says plainly that publishing from chat is not ready and offers the Publish button. A command whose control is off or locked says so and names the control; none fails silently.
# Typing "@" opens the mention menu in sections (Slides · Element · Files · Templates · Themes). A pick writes a readable token (@[File: name], @[Template: name], @[Theme: name]) and, on send, adds a typed reference to user_message.data.references; /add-slide, /duplicate and /delete add data.command; the caps mentions2 and commands1 are advertised only with this flag on (lib/studio-chat-commands-wire.ts is the whole wire; the Director side is DIRECTOR_MDC_MENTIONS_COMMANDS_ENABLED).
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_COMMANDS="false"

# STUDIO DECK SYNC TRUTH (FRONTEND-2, B26; E2E-2's finding of 27 Oct on Studio dev). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then the Builder is exactly as before. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy.
# On: after chat deletes and a page reload the rail header ("Slides N") and the footer ("Slide i / N") show the deck's real slide count, the one the viewer itself reports, instead of the larger count the session row kept
# from the build (the count is raised only while a build is in progress); and "This deck changed in another tab" is no longer drawn for a change nobody made in another tab: a difference found within 15 s of a change
# announced on this tab (Director's deck_mutation, or the tab's own edit) refreshes the deck quietly when nothing is unsaved, and any other difference shows only if it is still there 4 s later and reads "This deck was updated".
# "In another tab" stays for a message another tab sent. The session row follows too: after a chat change to a finished deck (Director's deck_mutation, an undo included) the Decks page card and the session list say the deck's real slide
# count, not the larger count the build wrote (a build in progress keeps today's rule). Acts with NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_DECK_CHANGED_NOTICE (the notice) and NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_DECK_MUTATION_REFRESH_ENABLED (Director's deck_mutation reaches the page). No Director change.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_DECK_SYNC_TRUTH="false"

# STUDIO BUILD FAILURE END (FRONTEND-2; E2E-2 chat parity Pass A, 27 Oct). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then the build state behaves exactly as today. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy.
# On: when Director's turn opens "Building your slides..." with a status update, no build frame (build_phase, build_event, slide_built) arrives while it is on screen, and the turn then ends with a chat message (Director's reply
# that the content could not be generated), Studio leaves the building state: no "0 of N built", no Pause / Stop, no "Building slides" under the composer, and Director's reply is the last word. A build that sends build frames, a
# paused or stopped build, a build accepted with the button and a deck that is built are never touched. No new text, no Director change.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_BUILD_FAILURE_END="false"

# STUDIO PAUSED LABEL (FRONTEND-2; PROGRAM-1 GO 27 Oct). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then the build ribbon reads exactly as today. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy.
# On: while a build is paused (its control state is paused) the build ribbon's headline reads "Paused", the label the build already has for that phase, instead of "Building your slides…" when a later status moved the phase back to building.
# Only the headline: the icon, the timer, the "N of M built" count and the Resume / Stop buttons are as today. No new text, no Director change.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_PAUSED_LABEL="false"

# STUDIO CHAT PARITY (FRONTEND-1; P3-1 A post-Thursday rows, Studio half; contract: deckster-workspace streams/frontend1/chat-parity-p3/CONTRACTS.md, DIRECTOR-2 GO 27 Oct). Three switches, one per row
# group, each on only for the string "true"; all default off, and then chat sends, socket handling and the Builder page are byte for byte what they were. Build-time values: change them on
# Vercel and redeploy. Each pairs with a Director flag of its own (DIRECTOR_MDC_THEME_LIBRARY_ENABLED / _IDENTITY_ / _TEMPLATES_). Rows 105 / 106 / 108 (notes, script,
# references) ride NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_ELEMENT_EDIT's single notes_updated path (#522, cap notes1); this change only lets a chat-written script or references draft go too.
# With a group on, each user_message adds the group's cap to client_caps (themes1 / identity1 / templates1), Director's studio_action {request_id, group, action, presentation_id, args, label} is
# taken out of band (never the transcript) and run through the SAME function the click path runs, and studio_action_result {request_id, status: done | failed | dismissed, error_code} answers it on the
# delivering socket (only "done" is success; Director closes the turn with its own line). A request for a group that is off answers failed / flag_off at once.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_PARITY_THEMES: rows 56 / 57 / 58 / 59 / 61. Director's set_theme_fonts {font_family?, font_family_heading?} (the font-selection feature's own eight families; needs
# NEXT_PUBLIC_THEME_FONT_SELECTION_ENABLED), save_theme {name, set_standard?}, set_standard_theme {theme_id}, clear_standard_theme, rename_theme {theme_id, name} (needs the Themes page's
# rename route, the one its own manage flag turns on) and apply_saved_theme {theme_id} run the composer palette's own library writes and the theme picker's own apply (a built deck is answered from
# its theme sync, as the chat theme directive; a build, an outline, a template reuse or Template Mode refuse it as theme_locked), then the palette re-reads its list. Themes are always named by
# id (Director resolves a name from its own store). Deleting a saved theme stays on the Themes page (row 60: declined by Director). THIS WRITES THE THEME LIBRARY AND THE DECK'S THEME.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_PARITY_THEMES="false"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_PARITY_IDENTITY: rows 62 / 63 / 64. Director's set_footer {template?, title?, date?, author?}, clear_footer, set_logo {image_url (https), alt_text?}, remove_logo and
# generate_logo {prompt} run the Master panel's own path (Show → Master…: the viewer opens it, its own read fills the fields, the request's fields are set as if typed, the Save button's own handler
# writes the footer and logo to every slide and closes it); set_deck_identity {company?, confidentiality?, logo_url?} runs the presenter-details dialog's own writer (needs NEXT_PUBLIC_DECK_IDENTITY_ENABLED),
# so the next message carries them as the user's own deck_identity. Every value is the user's own text (Director passes it verbatim, never invents it). Uploading a logo file stays on the panel (declined
# by Director). Clear footer and remove logo need no confirm (chat undo restores them). THIS WRITES THE DECK'S FOOTER AND LOGO.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_PARITY_IDENTITY="false"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_PARITY_PAID_LOGO: row 63's generate is one paid image call. A sub-flag under IDENTITY (both must be "true"), off until PK rules on paid chat actions: off, generate_logo is
# answered flag_off and nothing is charged; on, a Studio toast asks first ("Generate" within 30 s, else nothing runs), then the panel's own Generate handler and Save.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_PARITY_PAID_LOGO="false"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_PARITY_TEMPLATES: rows 65 / 67 / 76 (and 70 / 75 under the two sub-flags below). Director's select_template {template_id} runs the template picker's own select (the next
# message carries template_id as a picked template does; refused while build selections are locked), composer_template_action {template_id, action: use_original | rebuild | new_topic} opens the
# composer library dialog with that action, which runs it as the composer popup's pick does (each starts a NEW deck; Director sends it after its new-session directive), and rename_template
# {template_id, name} runs the Templates page's own rename (its manage route). Templates are always named by id (Director resolves a name from its own store). Rows 66 (New topic / Reuse as-is) and 72
# (apply a template to the open deck) have no live click path at this head and are answered unsupported; upload, preview, Template Mode, delete and the template story stay on their pages (declined by
# Director). THIS CHANGES THE NEXT BUILD'S TEMPLATE, THE TEMPLATE LIBRARY, AND CAN OPEN A NEW DECK.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_PARITY_TEMPLATES="false"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_PARITY_PAID_SAVE_TEMPLATE / NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_PARITY_PAID_OPTIMIZE: rows 70 / 75 are composer jobs (paid). Sub-flags under TEMPLATES (both must be "true"), off until
# PK rules on paid chat actions: off, save_template {name} and optimize_template {template_id} are answered flag_off and nothing runs; on, a Studio toast asks first (its one action within 30 s, else
# nothing runs), then the Save Template dialog's own save (the completed deck of this session) or the Templates page's own Optimize.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_PARITY_PAID_SAVE_TEMPLATE="false"
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_PARITY_PAID_OPTIMIZE="false"

# STUDIO CHAT ELEMENT EDIT 2 (FRONTEND-2, B32; PROGRAM-1 GO 27 Oct; E2E-2's element-edit run on Studio dev). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then chat element edit (NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_ELEMENT_EDIT) behaves exactly as today. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy.
# On, two fixes: (1) after a page reload an edit on the shown slide works: the runner checks the directive's slide_id against the shown deck's own ids and count, read from Layout's slide inventory (the session's restored slide list holds Director's outline ids, which are not Layout's, so every edit
# answered SLIDE_CHANGED); a slide that really changed still answers SLIDE_CHANGED, and when Layout's ids cannot be read the index check stands alone. (2) the element reference a send carries (and the "@" Element entry) is dropped when the deck changes under it (an Undo, a restored deck) or
# the shown slide is not the one it was selected on, and is written on every selection, so a stale hidden reference cannot follow the user. No Director change, no new text.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_ELEMENT_EDIT_2="false"

# STUDIO MODEL CHOICE DECK SAVE (FRONTEND-2, B37; E2E-2's F8 re-check on Studio dev, 27 Oct). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then model choice (NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_MODEL_CHOICE) behaves exactly as today. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy.
# On, two fixes to model choice saves, "This presentation" and "Reusable defaults": (1) a save is no longer refused 412 when the browser's If-Match is the router's own tag in another form (Vercel sends the router's strong tag on as W/"..."): Studio's stale-read check compares the
# opaque tags, a really different tag (another tab saved first) is still refused, and the router still gets its own tag as If-Match; (2) the picker says "Saved to your account" only after a save the account confirmed, the words of a failed save (changed elsewhere, refused, not available) after one that failed, and nothing before a save. No router change, no new text.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_MODEL_CHOICE_DECK_SAVE="false"

# STUDIO CLEAN CHAT ORDER (FRONTEND-2, B31; E2E-2's finding of 27 Oct on Studio dev, session c737ffe5). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then the chat is byte for byte what it was. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy. It needs NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_CLEAN and the Studio shell (the thread it orders is the v3.1 chat); without them it does nothing.
# On: (1) the job card's one line is no longer the last progress line of work that has ended ("Packaging your outline and picking a theme…" under "Waiting for you", then under "Building slides"): it closes when the phase, the outline or the newest approval card changes, and shows nothing at the outline gate; (2) the thread's notes (Stopped / Paused / Resumed markers, the user's directions) are drawn where they happened, between Director's replies, not after the last one.
# No new text, no Director change, nothing sent.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_CHAT_CLEAN_ORDER="false"

# STUDIO MODEL CHOICE PREFS VERSION (FRONTEND-2, B37 follow-up; E2E-2's capture of 28 Oct 02:15-02:17Z on Studio dev). On for the exact value "true"; default off, and then model choice (NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_MODEL_CHOICE, with the deck save flag) behaves exactly as today. Build-time value: change it on Vercel and redeploy.
# On, a model choice save carries the read's version in its own request header (X-Prefs-Version), never in If-Match: Vercel's edge applies If-Match to the function's response and swaps in its own 412 error page for a save that was written. The routes read the header
# (If-Match still accepted), compare it as an opaque tag, and send it back on every answer; a really stale read is still Studio's JSON 412. A 412 that is not Studio's JSON reads the choices again instead of saying "changed elsewhere". No router change, no new text.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_MODEL_CHOICE_PREFS_VERSION="false"
